From b129397b4e4ae06d63e3756eb541ebb275dd93c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:57:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Include the standard headers that are used, for newer libc++

The Windows build (MSYS2 clang64, newest packages on every run) stopped in
src/network/artic_base: std::vector used without #include <vector>. Newer
libc++ versions no longer pull such headers in through others. A scan of
src/ found 100 places in 82 files that use std::vector, std::string,
std::string_view, std::optional, std::atomic, std::array, std::mutex,
std::chrono, std::tuple, std::map, std::unordered_map, std::thread,
std::set, std::deque, std::span or std::condition_variable without
including its header, directly or through one of the project's own
headers. Each now includes it, outside any #if block.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
